From be05401a945c869504314d4db8e76aee7a4a1ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:51:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: six ways to win, with domination and the score winner
 at the last turn in Lua

game.ruleset writes out endspaceship (the ship must arrive), sets
endturn 475 (the year 2050 on this calendar) and lowers the culture win
to 8000 points with a 50% lead over the runner-up (sandbox: 20000 and
double, which no player reached). script.lua adds two rules on
turn_begin: domination, for a player who holds 60% of the land tiles
and 50% of all citizens for three turns running (checked from turn
100), and the score winner, named at the start of the last turn so the
game ends with a victor rather than a turn-limit notice. Both call
edit.player_victory; the thresholds are globals so a test can override
them. README.civ45 and the summary list the six wins. Conquest, the
allied win and culture are the server's own rules.
---
 data/civ45/README.civ45 |  10 ++++
 data/civ45/game.ruleset |  24 +++++++---
 data/civ45/script.lua   | 103 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 130 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

