+- Six ways to win. Conquest: every rival is dead or has surrendered.
+  Domination: hold 60 percent of the land tiles and 50 percent of the
+  world's citizens for three turns running, checked from turn 100 by the
+  ruleset's script. Culture: 8000 culture points and half again as much
+  as the runner-up (sandbox asks 20000 and double). Space: a spaceship
+  that arrives (endspaceship enabled). Alliance: the last alliance
+  standing wins together. Score: the game ends after turn 475 (the year
+  2050) and at the start of that turn the living player with the highest
+  score is named the winner, so the game ends with a victor rather than a
+  turn-limit notice. The thresholds are first values, untuned.
 - Strategic resources: Legion needs Iron and Armor needs Oil somewhere in
   the city's radius.
 - Nation-unique units and buildings: Aztec Jaguar Warrior (replaces
